    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.jump2d\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen jumping to a unique target, I get the following error message: \r\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua: ...Packages/start/echasnovski-mini.nvim/lua/mini/jump2d.lua:846: table index is nil\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        ...Packages/start/echasnovski-mini.nvim/lua/mini/jump2d.lua:846: in function 'spots_to_extmarks'\r\n        ...Packages/start/echasnovski-mini.nvim/lua/mini/jump2d.lua:783: in function 'spots_show'\r\n        ...Packages/start/echasnovski-mini.nvim/lua/mini/jump2d.lua:402: in function 'start'\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.0\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Write a file with contents like: \r\n\r\n```\r\na b c d\r\ne f g h\r\ni j k l\r\nm n o p\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. Attempt to jump to the letter `g`.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nIf there is only one possible target, the jump should go directly there.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nThrows the aformentioned error message.",
